                                                "example_id": "74bdb7e8-96d6-4616-a8fa-4f8632cc5d8f",
                                                "sense_id": "d0961385-26cd-34f3-973a-1e9eac77db6a",
                                                "text": "ante 1800, old proverb\nEngland were but a fling / Save for the crooked stick and the grey goose wing."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "fling",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ebb8de9d-a3ff-38d9-9ada-dfb952d3228b",
                                        "entry_id": "e99cc950-e4ae-33de-b37e-a9393106dbd1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To throw with violence or quick movement; to hurl."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "96498483-fbb4-4fb4-977c-380957927844",
                                                "sense_id": "ebb8de9d-a3ff-38d9-9ada-dfb952d3228b",
                                                "text": "'Tis Fate that casts the Dice, and as she flings,\nOf Kings makes Pedants, and of Pedants Kings."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "17ea5027-39d1-4b88-b41c-7b70bbfaf553",
                                                "sense_id": "ebb8de9d-a3ff-38d9-9ada-dfb952d3228b",
                                                "text": "I know thy generous temper well. / Fling but the appearance of dishonour on it, / It straight takes fire."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "15a364ca-1507-4137-927a-f3f7101fa4ea",
                                                "sense_id": "ebb8de9d-a3ff-38d9-9ada-dfb952d3228b",
                                                "text": "Wilkinson was struggling, sending the re-start straight into touch and flinging a pass the same way, and France then went close to the first try of the contest as Clerc took a long pass out on the left and was just bundled into touch by the corner flag."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "814da95b-7636-417c-8996-06f62b0b7488",
                                                "sense_id": "ebb8de9d-a3ff-38d9-9ada-dfb952d3228b",
                                                "text": "Signalman Bridges was killed by the blast, as was fireman Nightall. Amazingly, driver Gimbert came round some 200 yards away, on the grass outside the Station Hotel where he had been flung."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c36c9490-ba9c-3168-97af-431c18bd54e1",
                                        "entry_id": "e99cc950-e4ae-33de-b37e-a9393106dbd1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To move (oneself) abruptly or violently; to rush or dash."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7e6ca79d-ad0d-4635-882d-23fddf02f5e6",
                                                "sense_id": "c36c9490-ba9c-3168-97af-431c18bd54e1",
                                                "text": "And crop-full, out of doors he flings."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "feb9f5b6-6ef8-46c0-ab8d-1d6e980e34b8",
                                                "sense_id": "c36c9490-ba9c-3168-97af-431c18bd54e1",
                                                "text": "I see, sir, said I, I see what a man I am with. […] And away I flung, leaving him seemingly vexed, and in confusion."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c56a5ef6-67bc-447e-9617-f0e631043eeb",
                                                "sense_id": "c36c9490-ba9c-3168-97af-431c18bd54e1",
                                                "text": "I flung closer to his breast, / As sword that, after battle, flings to sheath."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "933f58e0-a952-430d-82e3-b27bf804d5a8",
                                                "sense_id": "c36c9490-ba9c-3168-97af-431c18bd54e1",
                                                "text": "\"We beseech your Majesty—\" said Glozelle, but Miraz had flung out of the tent and they could hear him bawling out his acceptance to Edmund."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7d3b71a3-fc7d-35bc-a743-89fe5e802cb1",
                                        "entry_id": "e99cc950-e4ae-33de-b37e-a9393106dbd1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To throw; to wince; to flounce."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "55a7460c-2550-4fcc-a22a-b67ddd0fa6a1",
                                                "sense_id": "7d3b71a3-fc7d-35bc-a743-89fe5e802cb1",
                                                "text": "The horse flung most potently, making his heels fly aloft in the air."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e85409f9-8ec6-362d-8da6-b487a7c913e0",
                                        "entry_id": "e99cc950-e4ae-33de-b37e-a9393106dbd1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To utter abusive language; to sneer."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "86c7ec6b-0782-455b-be3f-4fb435d92fdf",
                                                "sense_id": "e85409f9-8ec6-362d-8da6-b487a7c913e0",
                                                "text": "The scold began to flout and fling."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
